        <briefdescription>
<para>Prepares a text for a single TAP line. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each line break (<computeroutput>\\n</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>\\r</computeroutput>, or the <computeroutput>\\r\\n</computeroutput> pair) is replaced by a space, so that the text does not end the line. When <computeroutput>escape</computeroutput> is true, each <computeroutput>\\</computeroutput> is written as <computeroutput>\\\\</computeroutput> and each <computeroutput>#</computeroutput> as <computeroutput>\\#</computeroutput>, as the TAP 14 specification recommends for the test point descriptions and the reasons, so that a <computeroutput>#</computeroutput> in the text does not start a directive (for example <computeroutput># TODO</computeroutput>, which would hide a failure). The <computeroutput># Subtest:</computeroutput> comments are not escaped, since the specification defines no escapes in comments, and the node-tap parser uses their text as it is.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>text</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The text to prepare. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>escape</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to escape the <computeroutput>\\</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>#</computeroutput> characters. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The text, without line breaks, and escaped if requested. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
