        <definition>std::string micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::detail::anonymous_namespace{reporter-tap.cpp}::yaml_double_quoted</definition>
        <argsstring>(std::string_view text)</argsstring>
        <name>yaml_double_quoted</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::detail::anonymous_namespace{reporter-tap.cpp}::yaml_double_quoted</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>std::string_view</type>
          <declname>text</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Formats a text as a YAML double-quoted scalar. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The text is enclosed in <computeroutput>"</computeroutput>, with each <computeroutput>\\</computeroutput> written as <computeroutput>\\\\</computeroutput>, each <computeroutput>"</computeroutput> as <computeroutput>\\"</computeroutput>, and each control character (including the line breaks, the tab, and <computeroutput>DEL</computeroutput>) as a YAML escape sequence (<computeroutput>\\0</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>\\t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>\\n</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>\\r</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>\\e</computeroutput>, and so on, or <computeroutput>\\xHH</computeroutput> for the others), so that the value is a single line, and is valid YAML whatever it contains. As plain scalars, the values starting with <computeroutput>{</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>[</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>&apos;</computeroutput>, or containing <computeroutput>: </computeroutput> or <computeroutput> #</computeroutput>, would be rejected or truncated by the YAML parsers used by the TAP consumers. The bytes above <computeroutput>0x7F</computeroutput> are written as they are, since they are expected to be parts of UTF-8 sequences.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>text</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The text to format. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The double-quoted scalar. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
